# Business & Valuation Audit Command

When the user says **"run business audit"**, **"business audit"**, **"run valuation audit"**, or **"valuation audit"**:

## Execution mode (required)

Run in **Agent** mode with writes enabled—not Ask mode, not read-only subagents. The audit **must** create or update markdown under `docs/audits/`. **"No code changes"** means do not modify application or library source (for example under `app/`); it does **not** mean skip writing the report.

## What to do

1. Launch one subagent (generalPurpose) with read-only disabled and instruct it to follow `docs/process/business-valuation-audit-process.md`.
2. Require output report at `docs/audits/business/YYYY-MM-DD-business-valuation-audit.md`.
3. Audit only. Do not make code changes.
4. After completion, summarize top findings and report location.

## References

- Process: `docs/process/business-valuation-audit-process.md`
- Reports: `docs/audits/business/`
